  faqs: [
    { question: "Does any school in Thrissur actually teach IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Not one that can currently be confirmed. No school inside Thrissur appears on the authorised IB World School list, and none is confirmed as a Cambridge International centre. Students here who are studying IB or IGCSE are typically enrolled in a recognised online school, continuing a curriculum they started elsewhere, or getting ready to join a Diploma school outside Kerala." },
    { question: "How does tutor matching actually work for a Thrissur family?", answer: "Tell us the programme or board, subject, level and exam series, and tutors who have genuinely taught that exact course get shortlisted. Location barely enters into it, since Thrissur has no local school to draw specialists from anyway; the part that does matter is confirming a lesson time against your evenings. A free trial always runs first, online." },
    { question: "We relocated to Thrissur and our child was already on an international curriculum. What now?", answer: "This comes up often, given how many banking, gold-trade and Ayurveda-sector families move to Thrissur for work. A tutor gets matched to the exact curriculum and level your child was already following, so the tutoring continues that path rather than restarting it." },
    { question: "Do your tutors ever visit a home in Thrissur?", answer: "No, and that is true everywhere apart from Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. In Thrissur, every lesson runs live online, one to one, over video with a shared whiteboard, which is genuine private tuition delivered at home, not a promise that a tutor turns up at your door." },
    { question: "Are both Cambridge and Edexcel IGCSE covered?", answer: "Yes. Cambridge students are matched down to the exact code and tier, Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620 for example, and Edexcel students by specification and Foundation or Higher tier, working from each board's own past papers and mark schemes throughout." },
    { question: "What actually decides how much a Thrissur family pays?", answer: "Programme and level, the subject, session length, and how recently the tutor has taught that syllabus, all fixed for your match before the trial and left unchanged afterward. HL Diploma work generally costs more than MYP or IGCSE Core. Online delivery removes any travel charge from the equation, and nothing here runs on a long-term contract." },
    { question: "Can we watch a lesson before we agree to anything?", answer: "Every match includes one, at no cost. Your child works through genuine syllabus content with the tutor, and a short plan for the first month follows the trial. Whether to continue, adjust the plan, or try a different tutor entirely is your call from that point on." },
    { question: "Will a tutor write any part of my child's Internal Assessment for them?", answer: "No, never, under any circumstance. Support covers choosing a workable research question, explaining what a criterion actually rewards, sanity-checking a data-collection plan, and giving honest feedback on drafts. The assessed work itself stays the student's, without exception." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects does IB Gram actually cover for Thrissur students?", answer: "The subjects Thrissur's small DP cohort genuinely needs: both Maths routes at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay guidance alongside whichever of these a student is taking." },
    { question: "Do you work with MYP or PYP students, or only the Diploma?", answer: "Both get equal attention. MYP support in Thrissur usually centres on criterion-based analysis in the sciences and in Language and Literature, plus keeping a Personal Project journal moving. PYP sessions build reading, writing and number confidence, working toward the research skills an eventual Exhibition will demand." },
    { question: "With no local school to compare it against, is online tutoring genuinely reliable here?", answer: "It is closer to the only realistic option than a compromise. With no confirmed IB or Cambridge school anywhere in Thrissur, the specialist a student actually needs almost certainly teaches from somewhere else in India. A shared whiteboard, live past papers and recorded explanations cover most of what an in-room tutor would." },
    { question: "How are tutors checked before we are ever introduced?", answer: "On qualifications, on how recently they have taught that exact subject and level, and on their approach to assessment criteria, all before any family meets them. Given how thin Thrissur's own base is, a tutor with genuinely current syllabus experience gets priority over a generalist. The trial class is where you confirm the fit for yourself." },
    { question: "When is the right point to start tutoring?", answer: "Right at the start of the course works best, Grade 9 for IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma, leaving room to close gaps before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades all arrive close together. A later start, even in the final year, can still help provided sessions stay tightly focused on high-value topics and past papers." },
    { question: "We're weighing a switch from CBSE to IGCSE. What actually needs work?", answer: "Usually exam technique, not content. Command words such as 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' need direct teaching, and coursework or IA planning habits need building from scratch, since CBSE rarely demands either. A school holiday spent on exactly this before the switch tends to pay off." },
    { question: "Does the tutoring schedule account for Pooram and the monsoon?", answer: "Yes, by default. Sessions are built around Thrissur Pooram's disruption each April and May, the June-September monsoon's effect on evenings, and Onam as a genuine calendar pause. Adding an extra weekly slot before an exam series is simple since nothing here depends on travel." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any school, board or curriculum body?", answer: "No, not with any school named on this page, and not with the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel either. Every tutor works to a student's own school calendar and to the relevant board's published syllabus." },
  ],

